# Exocortex — Master Plan (status archive)

Superseded status entries, wave narratives, and baselines moved
verbatim from master-plan.prd on 2026-10-10. Append-only; nothing
here authorizes anything — the live plan and its D-row table are the
authority.

**Prior status (2026-10-06, v0.5.0 SHIPPED — the standalone-reliability
release):** version bumped (24 workspace dep reqs + the openapi golden
regenerated), CI's four shards green on the exact release tree, tag
v0.5.0 pushed (release.yml: correctness + all three platform builds +
assets green), and ALL 17 crates published to crates.io at 0.5.0
(publish exit 0, its own full matrix green inside the run). Two
release-cut catches, both the guard classes existing for: D40's
dreams→ops/cache dev-deps tripped the forward-dev-dep guard (dreams
joined STRIP_CRATES, the REL3 remedy) and one D36-class contention
flake (stub spawn stalled past a 3s deadline under 23 parallel jest
workers — deadline stretched to 20s). Release-note honesty, as the
PUBLISHING entry records: live Falkor/Redis/Postgres/CDC legs and the
SaaS adapter live suites not executed; compose chaos not run; D45's
real-data diagnosis ran on the owner's machine and its fix ships.
REL2 landed first (measured baseline, seam suites reusing the workspace
feature build, CI sharded to four parallel jobs — wall ~17min vs
~40min, all green). The queue after the release: PLT1 on the owner's
go, Wave 5 D3/D15, D19 still parked on LINEAR_API_KEY.

**Status (2026-10-02, ROUND 14 — the cascade's deep review, fixed in
cycle):** the deep-pr-review-lean pass over the five-commit cascade
returned changes-requested (7 Blocking, 26 Advisory — verify's store
rows read the wrong directory under the wrapper's falkordb layout,
--install-block could destroy an unreadable instruction file, the
harness row false-greened on two substrings, an unterminated marker
duplicated the block, the SSE error-body read hung unbounded behind a
wedged proxy, attach.json admitted a userinfo bypass and shell
injection, and the attached WAL slot leaked credential-bearing trees
while stranding pending writes). ALL fixed with named tests; the round
doc (`docs/reviews/round-14-review.prd`) carries every finding,
disposition, and the lens roster. Two boundaries recorded with
measurements (a 33s TMPDIR sweep reverted; conf-file foreign writers
out of client-side reach). A second-opinion/--final pass is reserved
for the loop's convergence check.

**Status (2026-10-02, GitHub issues #2–#7 triaged as D44–D49; D44-S1,
D45-partial, D46, D47, D48, D49, D44-S2 landed — the cascade is
closed):** the standalone multi-instance cascade from
the owner's dogfood. D44 S1 (a71cf3e): the supervised store runs
behind a watchdog shell in its own process group — an orphaned store
reaps itself when its node dies, even under kill -9 — teardown signals
the group, and `spawn_supervised` takes an exclusive flock on the data
dir so a second live store is refused naming the remedy; fail-without-it
tests for all three, one dependency (libc, rule-9 recorded). D45 (9d1137b, d66d641): post-startup store
deaths now carry exit status + log tail at ERROR level (visible under
the default filter); the repro harness is landed (env-gated live:
control leg asserts, dual-writer leg manufactures the #2 hazard,
save-policy discriminator, real-data mode, scale knob) — synthetic
corpora to ~3M nodes did NOT reproduce, so the row PARKS ON the owner
running it over a copy of the real data dir; root cause unconfirmed.
D46 (4a67f2c, c10b7fc): every redis-plane store consumer now rides a
ConnectionManager (feature flag on the existing redis dep) — the fire
drain, discovery delivery, post-ingest effects, and the health probe
all survive a supervised restart; red/green fail-without-it proven.
D47 (62ba60d, issue #5 closed): all ten binaries log WARN by
default (RUST_LOG overrides), the hydration timeout carries the
backend's own HTTP status + bounded body, and a degraded backend
stamps reads with a `sync` health object + a new `backend_status`
tool — a frozen snapshot never reads as live again. D48 (884987c,
issue #7 closed): the installer seeds Claude Code's ~/.claude/skills
via symlink, --dump-block emits version-marked block, and
--install-block replaces the region in place — reruns never
duplicate; the 300-word gate now binds the emitted form (299/300).
D49 (19f9ece, issue #6 closed): --verify grew its four missing
rows — orphaned/foreign store processes on the data dir (ps scan +
lock-holder liveness), the stale `port` artifact (PINGed, kept for
S2), the PRD-S6-promised harness row (RED when unwired), and the
org/user partition mismatch (WAL-stamped ledger naming the live
pairs). D45 CLOSED 2026-10-05 (root cause + fix in the installation repair):
the store death was the `--save 1 1` BGSAVE fork SIGILLing the parent
over the loaded real graph — supervised stores now disable the RDB
snapshot (AOF everysec carries durability), the owner's local install
is repaired and boots clean on the real 1,644-node graph (issue #3 to
close with the row). D44-S2 (13d1ec6, issue #2 closed): a second concurrent
mcp-standalone session on one data dir now ATTACHES to the live node
(typed lock error → attach.json endpoint+secrets → gRPC
liveness+fingerprint probe → owner credentials + per-session WAL
slot in client mode) instead of failing — concurrent sessions are
finally the normal case, one store per data dir by construction; the
verify store row counts DISTINCT PORTS (redis rewrites its title; a
naive pid scan double-counted the watchdog shells). Issue #3 stays
open against its row.
**Next, in order:** the release cut waits on the owner's version
call; D45's real-data run is one command recorded in its row; then
the standing queue (PLT1 on the owner's go, Wave 5 D3/D15, REL2,
D33).

