**Status (2026-09-05, CLI2+CLI3 SHIPPED — the CLI as the non-MCP
client bridge, plus the suggested-surface reconciliation):** CLI2: the
inspiration for CLI1 was Perplexity-class clients (shell commands, no
MCP); `exocortex-cli --dump-block` now prints the pasteable
instruction block for those clients' custom instructions (207 words,
bounded + content-tested; the gen-playbook folding is the recorded
follow-up if it drifts), and every command carries `--json` as the
machine contract. CLI3: an external client-suggestion pass (query
--cypher / get / search / upsert --json / link / delete / export
--since / stats) was reconciled against the hard rules. ACCEPTED and
shipped: `add --link Kind:<32-hex-id>` (repeatable; the §4.5
cross-batch edge via `EdgeHintInput.to_memory_id` — smoke-proven: the
neighborhood carries the linked row) and `add --draft @file` (the
upsert --json equivalent; the file's type must agree with the
positional). REFUSED, with the rule cited: raw `--cypher` (CR-10:
Cypher never leaves exocortex-storage, and a raw passthrough bypasses
visibility scoping — search/get/related/chain are the typed
equivalents) and `delete` (the store is append-only and bi-temporal;
no producer delete surface exists by design, the D20-recorded
boundary — supersession and edge retraction are the model's tools).
RECORDED as follow-ups: an `export` passthrough (the node's
`--export`/`--export-corpus` already exist) and `stats` (needs a
counts op; `memories_in_region` is region-bounded). Evidence:
cli_smoke edge round trip + the block's bounded-and-complete unit test (the bin's other 4 unit tests cover rendering/args).

**Status (2026-09-05, CLI1 SHIPPED — exocortex-cli, the human face
beside MCP; smoke-proven round trip):** `exocortex-cli` (a bin target
inside exocortex-client): reads (`search`, `get`, `related`, `chain`)
ride the node's HTTP operations with bearer auth — CR-9 parity with
MCP by construction — and `add` reuses `EndSessionTool` verbatim (the
same signed submit path agents use, pinned to `session://cli` so admin
policy can scope it). Type labels render from the same composed
ontology. `--json` for machines. The landing re-proved two standing
lessons: pack crates nothing references are dead-stripped (the CLI
initially validated against dev-v1 alone and rejected an `Insight` —
the D27 black_box links now live in the CLI), and an in-process node
under a current-thread test runtime deadlocks the moment a test blocks
on a child process (`multi_thread`, the eof-drain precedent). Smoke:
`tests/cli_smoke.rs` spawns the REAL binary against an in-process node
— add accepted, search renders `[Insight] <title>`, get returns the
row — plus 4 unit tests on rendering/args.

**Status (2026-09-05, LP1 SHIPPED — the study pack, the third
ontology; fingerprint moved deliberately; matrix green 201 oks):**
`crates/exocortex-pack-study-v1` composes beside dev-v1 and ln-v1 in
every binary: 7 memory types (LearningGoal, Topic, Resource,
StudySession, ReviewSession, Insight, Question), 3 entity types
(Subject, Author, Provider), 11 kinds (Pursues, PrerequisiteFor,
Progresses, Covers, About, StudiedFrom, Answers, Raises,
FoundDifficult, Reinforces + computed-only ClusteredWith), rules L1-L3
(transitive prerequisites, answer-source, indirect progress). Two
design facts the landing proved, both pinned by tests: pack insertion
order is NAME-SORTED with per-pack id offsets, so a third pack's name
must sort after the second's or it renumbers the second's ids (the
study name was chosen for exactly this; the composition test pins
no-renumbering for both prior packs), and duplicate type names across
packs are registration errors (Provider, not Institution — ln-v1 owns
that name). **The authorized fingerprint move:
`4615018b…96c4` → `9f92957f…69c9`** (a superset event under OC-PRD;
AGENTS, CLAUDE, and this plan updated in-commit; playbook regenerated
at 72 kinds / 68 assertable; seam inventory 41). Evidence:
