**Status (2026-09-02, Wave 2 LOCALLY COMPLETE — D17 shipped):** The
probabilistic half of entity resolution landed as
`crates/exocortex-entity-resolution` — the half D13's deterministic
join deliberately excludes ("Acme Financial Corp" vs "acme financial
corporation"). Classical Fellegi-Sunter, no learning system, no new
dependency (serde/anyhow only; the comparators — Jaro-Winkler, token
set, legal-suffix stripping — are hand-written in-crate): m/u
probabilities per comparison feature estimated from an
operator-labelled pair set with Laplace smoothing, summed
log-likelihood-ratio scoring, and decision thresholds CALIBRATED
from the labelled scores themselves (midpoint boundary, accept at
3/4 toward the match mean, review at 3/4 toward the non-match mean —
magic constants cannot mean the same thing across feature counts).
Missing attributes are a third comparison state, not evidence
either way; a feature with match-only evidence refuses estimation
("label pairs that exercise it"); calibration requires both classes.
Matches are PROPOSALS (match/review/non_match JSONL via the
`exocortex-er` binary) — the harness never writes a graph; D13's
join remains the only automatic identity. The evaluation harness
(precision/recall/F1 + confusion over the labelled set) IS the
deliverable; corpus input is JSONL shaped exactly like the
`--export-corpus` lineage output. 13 tests (10 lib + 3 harness:
round-trip F1=1.0 on a clean set, the singular/plural boundary lands
in review not match, binary evaluate/classify against real files,
label/id validation, blocking never pairs key-disjoint records).
Wave 2's locally-satisfiable rows are now ALL closed (D21, D18, D13,
PX4, D1, D17); D19 alone remains, parked on owner credentials. Next
per directive 7: the Wave 2 boundary review round.

**Status (2026-09-02, closing — D1 COMPLETE; Wave 2 remainder D17):** The
Delta flavor landed as `crates/exocortex-adapter-delta` and closes D1:
the `_delta_log` transaction log replayed DIRECTLY (JSON commits +
single AND multi-part parquet checkpoints with the classic nested
action columns) — no new external dependency (the log is serde_json +
