treated as a hint with the file scan authoritative. Hermetic suite
(10 tests): JSON-log replay, checkpoint+commits equivalence, multi-part
completeness from the part names (a missing part fails closed),
percent-escaped paths, protocol refusals, mock-server end-to-end under
the TABLE flavor, version advance + regression refused. D1 is now
CLOSED across all three flavors (parquet-dir, iceberg, delta) with the
shared declared-projection core in `exocortex-adapter-table` and the
adapter-contract gate claiming all three (16 obligations). Wave 2
remainder: D17 (locally satisfiable); D19 parked on credentials.

**Status (2026-09-02, latest — D1 iceberg flavor shipped):** The
iceberg milestone of D1 landed as `crates/exocortex-adapter-iceberg`:
a local Iceberg table's CURRENT snapshot as a bounded declared-
projection import under the `iceberg` TABLE flavor, reading the format
directly — `metadata.json`, Avro manifest lists/manifests, Parquet
data files — with no catalog client and no engine. The direct reader
is a recorded decision (PUBLISHING.md): the official `iceberg` crate
stays deny-banned BY CHOICE (catalog/REST surface + a second arrow
line in a leaf binary), and apache-avro alone cannot read real v2
manifests anyway — Iceberg v2 keys partition struct fields by
field-id strings ("1000"), which Avro's name grammar forbids
(apache-avro: "Invalid field name 1000", reproduced in the suite), so
the adapter frames the object container itself (order-preserving
schema sanitization, positional decode, null+deflate codecs with the
zlib/raw container ambiguity handled both ways). Partition discipline:
identity-partitioned columns resolve from the MANIFEST partition
values when the writer omitted them from data files; non-identity
transforms (bucket/truncate/month) are derived values and are refused
for mapped columns, fail-closed naming the transform. Snapshot
identity is Iceberg's own `current-snapshot-id` (rewind refusal proven
in-suite). The declared-projection mapping core moved to
`exocortex-adapter-table` (one implementation for parquet-dir/iceberg/
delta — the R6-R286/287 no-divergence discipline), and the
adapter-contract gate claims the iceberg crate (15 obligations).
Dependency record per rule 9: apache-avro exact `=0.21.0` (rust-version
1.85.0, the workspace floor), flate2 (already in-tree) declared
directly, bon held to 3.9.3 in Cargo.lock (3.10 needs rustc 1.88).
Hermetic suite `crates/exocortex-adapter-iceberg/tests/iceberg_table.rs`
(10 tests): hand-framed v2 manifests (the digit-leading-key byte shape
real tables carry), genuine apache-avro-written v1 manifests (one
deflate-coded), overlay/absent-column, deleted entries, delete-file
refusal, empty table, remote-scheme fail-closed, mock end-to-end under
the TABLE flavor, new-snapshot + rewind. D1 remainder: the Delta
flavor, its own milestone with its own dependency record. Wave 2
remainder: D1(Delta)/D17; D19 parked on credentials.

