story in the row below): (1) relative `--loadmodule` paths resolve
against the DATA DIRECTORY (redis chdirs into `--dir` before loading
modules) — failed on every runner; `resolve_paths` now canonicalizes.
(2/3) the runtime's platform floors: darwin-arm64 `falkordb.so` declares
`minos 15.0` (macos-14 can never load it → arm64 leg on `macos-15`) and
linux-x64 `redis-server` needs `GLIBC_2.38` (ubuntu-22.04 native can't
→ the linux leg keeps its 22.04 builder for the shipped binaries' 2.35
floor and validates inside the digest-pinned falkordb/falkordb trixie
container). (4) the module dlopens Homebrew `libomp`/`openssl@3` at
absolute paths — now bundled beside the module as pinned ghcr.io bottle
blobs (last arm64_sequoia builds) and loaded via the store child's
`DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (standalone is genuinely self-contained on macOS
now). (5) the wrapper's background client lost its stdin under POSIX
async-list semantics (`<&0 &`) — now dup'd to fd 3 in the foreground.
Diagnosability shipped with each fix: a dying store names its exit
status plus its own log tail (stdout joined to the sink — redis logs
there), and missing runtime files fail fast by path. The queue behind D29 shrank by one the same day: **PX4 closed** (the
Mintlify adapter's first real-corpus run — 36 authored pages on the
canonical loanlight docs checkout, 92 memories / 94 relationships
through a live DocsAdapter-signed backend node, idempotent full replay,
UnknownType exercised on real input; two adapter defects fixed in its
repo — see the PX4 row). Remaining: D19/D1/D17 (Wave 2), then Wave 3's
PX5/D24/D6/D20.

**Status (2026-09-01, later — D28+D27 closed; release re-held on D29):**
Two dogfood/release defects closed this session and the full gate
matrix re-verified green (`scripts/verify-release.sh` exit 0, 23 gate
commands, 153 suite-oks; commits `8bdb5e1` D28, `07d4694` D27; main
pushed, v0.3.0 re-tagged at `07d4694`). **D28:** Crush dropped the
JSON-Schema `definitions` map while passing `$ref`s through, so models
guessed `end_session` draft fields (`missing field memory_type`) —
`tools/list` now inlines every ref (self-contained schemas) and the
instruction block names the exact draft fields. **D27:** root-caused to
rmcp's stdin-EOF shutdown dropping in-flight (and read-but-unpolled)
tool calls — NOT an HTTP/2 fault (h2 trace: ~40ms round-trip with
stdin open; both PRD hypotheses disproven). Fix: EOF-draining stdio
reader (quiet = no in-flight call AND no dispatch in 300ms grace,
55s budget), deterministic no-runtime regression (delaying proxy),
script sequencing write→commit→read (8/8 local runs). The re-tagged
release run (33543324895) then got PAST the old failure — invocation 1
passed — but failed at **D29**, a NEW defect: the packaged-standalone
validation's SECOND invocation died with `supervised redis-server
exited during startup` on the macos-14 runner (local runs of the same
script+runtime pass 8/8, so it is runner-or-sequence-specific; leading
suspicion: a port/process-cleanup race between the validation's two
back-to-back wrapper invocations). D29 holds the binaries; crates.io
is unaffected. Dogfood: `~/.cargo/bin/exocortex-mcp-client` reinstalled
with both fixes (loads at next Crush restart).

**Status (2026-09-01, D27 closed — v0.3.0 binaries unblocked):** The
standalone submit hang is root-caused and fixed: rmcp treats stdin EOF
as immediate shutdown, dropping in-flight (and read-but-unpolled) tool
calls — the live harness pipes its requests and closes stdin, so any
submit still on the wire lost its response. The wire path itself is
healthy (h2 frame trace: ~40ms round-trip with stdin held open); both
earlier hypotheses are disproven. Fix: an EOF-draining stdio reader
(quiet = no in-flight call AND no dispatch in the 300ms grace window,
bounded at 55s > the 20s+30s gRPC deadlines), a deterministic
no-runtime regression (`backend_eof_drain.rs`: in-process node behind a
400ms delaying proxy; fails-by-stash without the drain), and the live
script now sequences write→commit→read (8/8 clean runs). Next:
re-validate the release (`scripts/verify-release.sh`), re-tag v0.3.0.

**Status (2026-08-31, later — D28 closed):** Dogfood failure on the
write path: `end_session` calls from Crush failed deserialization
(`missing field memory_type`, then `missing field content`). Root cause:
schemars serves referenced draft types as `$ref`s beside a root
`definitions` map; Crush drops the map and passes the `$ref` through
unresolved, so the calling model guesses field names. Fix (D28):
`tools/list` now inlines every `#/definitions/X` ref — schemas are
self-contained for any harness — and the instruction block names the
exact draft fields (297 words). Fail-without-fix proven by stash.

